        <name>FileNameOffs</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::pdb::ModuleInfoHeader::FileNameOffs</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Array of [0..NumFiles) DBI name buffer offsets. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>In the reference implementation this field is a pointer. But since you can&apos;t portably serialize a pointer, on 64-bit platforms they copy all the values except this one into the 32-bit version of the struct and use that for serialization. Regardless, this field is unused, it is only there to store a pointer that can be accessed at runtime. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
